  "ceiling": "AUDIT_ONLY structural/stoichiometric second-signal for a NEW target property (hydroxyl value). It corroborates that the module's advancement variable n governs both EEW and OHV self-consistently across the pure DGEBA oligomer series (not curve-fit) and cleanly separates advancement secondary OH from phenolic/primary OH, but asserts nothing about the exact OHV of polydisperse commercial grades (measured composition required), product qualification, or cure conversion. Live runtime stays LOCKED_INTERNAL; the commercial_product_claim_locked=true lock is unchanged.",
  "claim": "An independent RDKit-2026.03.2 reference implementation adds a NEW molecular property to the module's canonical-structure-rule claim: the HYDROXYL VALUE (hydroxyl number) OHV of the linear DGEBA oligomer series, OHV(n) = 56100 * n / (M0 + n*M_repeat) in mg KOH/g (ASTM D4274 definition; M(KOH)=56.1056 g/mol). (1) The unadvanced n=0 DGEBA monomer carries ZERO titratable hydroxyls, so OHV(0)=0 exactly (structural anchor). (2) For each independently RDKit-built oligomer n=0..3, total -OH == n AND all n are secondary aliphatic (0 phenolic, 0 primary), giving OHV = [0, 89.79, 123.42, 141.02] mg KOH/g. (3) The series is monotone increasing and bounded above by the C18H20O3-repeat asymptote 56100/M_repeat = 197.29 mg KOH/g; the hydroxyl count equals the mass-advancement variable n for every oligomer, so OHV and EEW(n)=170.21+142.18n are two independent structural read-outs of ONE advancement state. (4) Four fail-closed controls (bisphenol-A 2 phenolic OH, glycidol 1 primary OH, neopentyl glycol 2 primary OH, fully-hydrolyzed DGEBA diol 2 primary+2 secondary OH) are all correctly excluded as non-advancement-series members. IUPAC-2021 standard-atomic-weight uncertainty propagates to <=0.0046 mg KOH/g on OHV(n=1), so the 0.5 mg KOH/g bar carries ~110x headroom. Corroborative only: asserts no exact OHV for polydisperse commercial grades (composition is measured, not derived) and modifies no live lock.",
